  "code": "1523",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 99.9989%;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 99.8607%;\"></colgroup>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>COMMENTS:</strong><br>Basophils are white blood cells that concentrate on dealing with allergic reactions. Higher than normal results of the absolute basophil count&nbsp;is called basophilia and may indicate Hives, Food allergy, Inflamation, Some forms of leukemia, Crohn&rsquo;s disease,&nbsp;Hypothyroidism, Hemolytic anemia.<br>Lower than normal results of the absolute basophil count is called basopenia and may indicate Severe allergies, Hypothyroidism.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
